WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:42.980
What is this?!

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.600
It’s a race! A race!

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.400
Go for it!

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:57.910
This is footage from the Pokémon Marine Athletics Race
currently being held in Minamo City.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.410
Marine Athletics?

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:05.250
It’s an open water obstacle course
for Pokémon.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.660
Huh...

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.440
As you can see, race days can be very thrilling,
and there’s no shortage of fans.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.780
It’s a Showers!

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.860
Eevee is cheering for Showers!

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.730
She may someday become one, after all.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:41.160
She’s a pretty mysterious Eevee.
She won’t evolve whatever we try.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:50.450
Eevee have unstable genes in general,
so maybe that one’s genes are more unstable than most.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.050
Or perhaps... Maybe she’s hesitant,
unable to decide what path she should take.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.560
Showers won!

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:15.740
Apparently that Showers
and that Laglarge are friendly rivals.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.810
You know a lot about it, Kikuna.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:22.110
Showers’ trainer is a friend of mine
from university.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.450
Really?!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:31.010
Contestants Kairi and Showers,
congratulations on your victory!

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:34.740
Eevee...

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.410
Do you want to meet Showers?

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:45.200
Can we go? I’d like to learn more
about Eevee’s evolutions, too!

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.390
That’s a good idea.
Learning that is important.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:53.150
I’ll contact Kairi. He’s a very welcoming guy,
so I’m sure he won’t mind.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.050
Me too! I wanna go, too!

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:55.860
So do I!

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.200
Very well!
Go and enjoy yourselves, everyone!

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.990
All right!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:37.780
Minamo City, Hoenn Region

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:41.210
This is Minamo City,
in the Hoenn Region.
Minamo City, Hoenn Region

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.090
A beautiful port city
surrounded by the sea.
Minamo City, Hoenn Region

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.090
So that’s the Marine Athletics
race course!

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.870
It looks huge when you’re
this close to it!

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.850
It’s like a floating theme park!

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.240
Um, we’re here to see Mr. Kairi...

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.940
In that case...
Try heading to the other side of that rock.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.030
He practices over there
all the time.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.330
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.570
Showers. Bubble Jet Pokémon.
Water type.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:29.720
It has evolved from the Normal-type Eevee
to be suitable for an aquatic life.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:37.600
Its cell composition is similar to water molecules.
As a result, it can melt away and hide itself in water.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.820
Hey, kids.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.920
You must be Koharu, Satoshi
and Go, right?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.660
Yeah!

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:51.140
And this is Koharu’s Eevee!

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.720
Mr. Kairi, congrats on winning
the Marine Athletics Race!

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.040
Congratulations!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.770
Thank you.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:03.300
From what Kikuna said,
it sounded like you want to hear all about Showers.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.990
Yes! I would love that!

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:07.990
It’d be my pleasure.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.090
Showers!

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.470
That’s Showers for you.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:39.670
The best way to learn about Showers
is to go swimming with it, you know.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.980
Oh, right.
Why don’t you enter the race?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:46.050
The Kids Marine Athletics Race
is tomorrow.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.550
That sounds fun!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.300
Yeah, I’ll do it!

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.970
For my partner...
I choose you!

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.020
Are you okay, Satoshi?!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.690
I-I’m fine.
This happens all the time.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.650
You tough guy, you...

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.050
Who’re you gonna choose
as your partner, Go?

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.520
I have so many,
it’s hard to decide.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.910
You wealthy guy, you...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.250
Okay! I choose you, Dewgong!

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.000
And you’re entering
with Eevee, Koharu?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.770
I don’t need a Water-type to enter?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.800
Course not!

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.580
Eevee! We can enter, too!

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.440
Uonoragon,
can’t you swim any faster?

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.010
Oh, come on...

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.100
It’s fast! And it’s... running?!

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.190
Sakurabyss?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.360
They're beautiful!

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.240
Sakurabyss! South Sea Pokémon!
Water type!

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:44.010
It lives at the bottom of the sea!
In the springtime, its pink body turns more vivid!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.200
Go!

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.880
Have you, have you perhaps maybe

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:17.260
grown up without me noticing?

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.920
Amazing!

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.710
Good job, Dewgong!
In the right-side pocket

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:21.630
In the right-side pocket

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:22.500
of your dusty old clothes

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.980
You tried...
of your dusty old clothes

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.680
You left the handheld adventure

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.150
that was everything to us

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:27.960
Nearly!
that was everything to us

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.110
that was everything to us

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.850
The memories from those days

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.820
are now looking for you!

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.420
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:40.900
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.720
Guess that really was too much.
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.060
Don’t let it get to you, Eevee!
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.030
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.020
So let’s go somewhere! Take me somewhere, anywhere!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.730
Calm down, Sarunori!
So let’s go somewhere! Take me somewhere, anywhere!

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.230
So let’s go somewhere! Take me somewhere, anywhere!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:57.460
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:58.810
Let’s have a fight!

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.410
1. Once the battle’s done

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.200
2. And we’re laughing or crying

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.130
On 3, let’s be friends!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:13.670
Any day and every day, that’s always been my rule

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:19.430
With this unpredictable, unfathomable world awaiting

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.890
Let’s go! Every time you trip and fall

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:26.170
Let’s go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.990
I choose you!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.160
Eevee looks really happy.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.650
She’s really looking up to Showers!

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:46.150
Koharu’s Eevee is cute.

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:47.870
It brings back memories.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:52.150
You’ve been raising your Showers
since it was an Eevee, Mr. Kairi?

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.040
Yeah.

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:57.950
Um... Mr. Kairi, why did your Eevee
evolve into a Showers?

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:04.120
Uh... If there was something that inspired you
to evolve it into Showers, please tell me!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.560
What inspired me, huh?

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.590
I’m a pro surfer.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.990
I always took Eevee along with me
when I went surfing.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:14.470
He was with me when training,
and even for tournaments.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.580
My Eevee really loved the sea,

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:21.210
so one day I got the idea
to sit him on my surfboard.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.600
Then...

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.550
You’re doing great, Eevee!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:35.400
So the evolution to Showers
just came naturally to both of us.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:49.130
I wonder what your Eevee
will evolve into.

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:50.810
That’s the problem...

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:59.690
Oh, really?
So that’s why you came here...

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.910
I don’t know if Eevee
wants to evolve but can’t,

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:06.200
or if she just wants to stay as she is...

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:10.640
But I’d like to learn all about
Eevee and its evolutions.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:11.870
You’re amazing, Koharu.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.810
You’re really thinking hard
about Eevee.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:20.170
So, what do you want her
to evolve into?

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.330
Showers? Thunders? Booster?

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.400
Eefee?! Blackie?

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:28.220
Leafia? Glacia?! Nymphia?!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.180
I don’t want to make that decision.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.390
I want Eevee to
choose her own path.

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:38.330
Rather than me or anyone
deciding for her.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:41.730
That’s what I’d want,
if I was Eevee.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.290
I see.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.700
I hope your feelings get through
to Eevee, Koharu.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:13:00.710
Now, it’s time for the junior event,
the Kids Marine Athletics Race, to begin!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.900
Let’s race each other, Satoshi!

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.180
You read my mind!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.280
I’m gonna win!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.180
No, me!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.480
Let’s go!

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.370
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.950
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.410
You’ve got it, Eevee!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.030
